<report>
<title>Relative risk meta-analysis</title>
<br />
<table>
<tr><th>Stratum</th><th colspan="4">Table (exposed +ve, control +ve, exposed -ve, control -ve)</th><th></th></tr>
<block name="inputs">
<tr><td>@st</td><td>@a</td><td>@b</td><td>@c</td><td>@d</td><td>@lb</td></tr>
</block>
</table>
<br />
<table>
<tr><th>Stratum</th><th>Relative risk</th><th colspan="2"><ci>@pc% CI (@method)</ci></th><th></th></tr>
<block name="risks">
<tr><td>@st</td><td>@{rr:roundu}</td><td><ci>@{lci:roundu}</ci></td><td><ci>@{uci:roundu}</ci></td><td>@lb</td></tr>
</block>
</table>
<br />
<table>
<tr><th>Stratum</th><th>Standardized effect</th><th>Variance</th><th colspan="2">% Weights (fixed, random)</th><th></th></tr>
<block name="risks">
<tr><td>@st</td><td>@{yi:roundu}</td><td>@{vi:roundu}</td><td>@{wt:roundu}</td><td>@{dwt:roundu}</td><td>@lb</td></tr>
</block>
</table>

<p><u>Fixed effects (Mantel-Haenszel, Rothman-Boice)</u><br />
Pooled relative risk = @{rr:roundu} (<ci>@pc% CI = @{from:roundu} to @{to:roundu}</ci>)<br />
Chi<sub>2</sub> (test relative risk differs from 1) = @{x2:roundu}  (df = @df)  <pval>@{xp:pval}</pval></p>

<p><u>Non-combinability of studies</u><br />
Cochran Q = @{qc:roundu}  (df = @df_cochran)  <pval>@{xp_cochran:pval}</pval><br />
Moment-based estimate of between studies variance = @{tausq:roundu}<br />
I<sub>2</sub> (inconsistency) = @isq% (<ci>@pc1% CI = @llisq% to @ulisq%</ci>) </p>

<p><u>Random effects (DerSimonian-Laird)</u><br />
Pooled relative risk = @{dsrr:roundu} (<ci>@pc% CI = @{dsll:roundu} to @{dsul:roundu}</ci>)<br />
Chi<sub>2</sub> (test relative risk differs from 1) = @{dsx2:roundu}  (df = @df_ds)  <pval>@{xp_ds:pval}</pval></p>

<p><u>Bias indicators</u></p>
<block name="egger">
<p>Begg-Mazumdar: Kendall's @tau  <pval>@{p2:pval}</pval><br />
Egger: bias = @a (<ci>@pc_egger% CI = @cl to @cu</ci>)  <pval>@{p:pval}</pval></p>
</block>
<block name="harbord">
<p>Harbord-Egger: bias = @a (<ci>@pc_harbord% CI = @cl to @cu</ci>)  <pval>@{p:pval}</pval></p>
</block>
</report>
